# Llama 3.2 Customer Support Fine-Tuning

## Overview

This project demonstrates Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) by adapting Meta's Llama 3.2 3B Instruct model for customer support using QLoRA. Instead of updating the entire model, lightweight LoRA adapters were trained, making the fine-tuning process significantly more memory efficient while maintaining strong performance.

---

## Motivation

After studying Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation, André wanted to explore the next step in LLM Engineering: fine-tuning open-source language models.

The goal was to understand the complete QLoRA workflow, from dataset preparation and model quantization to training, evaluation, and publishing the resulting LoRA adapter on the Hugging Face Hub.

